      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="699961478">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-07-08T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="836983">Coolcat21</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP733 Kensington Park

Posted: N53° 00.193' W112° 50.777'

MyGPSr: N53° 00.194' W112° 50.779'

(FOUND)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I stopped in to search for this one on my way through Camrose today. After I parked at N53° 00.085' W112° 50.775' and made my way in from the south, I saw the sentinel trees I'd seen in others' context photos. They're really the only thing that could serve to help determine the location of this one: it's smack dab in the middle of the grassy expanse.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After wandering for a bit, I was able to spy the hole &lt;strong&gt;YES!&lt;/strong&gt; and after removing a bunch of grass clippings, the cap was ready for the photo session.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the cap and the excuse to tour southwest Camrose, my first time here!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="693366375">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-06-10T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1565005">Takin it Easy</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP733 Kensington Park

Posted: N53° 00.193 W112° 50.777 

GPSr: N53° 00.193 W112° 50.778 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mrs. TiE and I were out running some errands between Stettler and Drumheller and made a detour in the rain up to Camrose to check out the Kensington Park cap.  The cap has no guard/marker posts, but I got lucky and spotted the hidey hole even with the grass cover.  To anyone watching, it must have been funny watching me in shorts, a tee short and sandals run out into a field in the pouring rain, kneel down on the ground, take a picture of what looks like grass and then boot back to the car.  Haha... I've done much sillier things for a cap find.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[FOUND]  Thanks for the cap vdD/OFTH!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
